    <section class="intro section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">HOME SERVER / NEXT CHAPTER</p>
      <h1>More services, same rules.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The machine is built. Now it gets useful, one private experiment at a time.</p>
      <div class="intro-links"><a class="button" href="#running">See what is running</a><a class="text-link" href="../">← Back to the build story</a></div>
    <button class="intro-scroll-cue" type="button" aria-label="Scroll to next section"></button></section>

    <section class="section-shell split-section">
      <div class="homelab-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">THE OPERATING RULE</p><h2>Every service earns its place.</h2></div>
        <div class="homelab-copy"><p>The platform is ready for self-hosted applications and local AI experiments. New services will be added one at a time, monitored from the start, and kept behind the same private access boundary.</p><p>Each service gets its own Compose project, a health check, useful metrics, resource limits, and a recovery plan. The goal is to learn how the system behaves, not to collect containers.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="running" class="section-shell">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">RUNNING NOW</p><h2>The first layer is already useful.</h2><p class="section-intro">These services form the current local platform. Add sanitized screenshots to the matching folders when you want to show the work visually.</p></div>
      <div class="story-grid service-grid">
        <button class="story-tile" data-service="compose"><span class="tile-number">01</span><span class="tile-icon">▣</span><strong>Docker Compose</strong><small>Repeatable containers without turning the server into a mystery box.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-service="prometheus"><span class="tile-number">02</span><span class="tile-icon">◒</span><strong>Prometheus</strong><small>Metrics make the quiet failures visible.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-service="grafana"><span class="tile-number">03</span><span class="tile-icon">◌</span><strong>Grafana</strong><small>Dashboards turn signals into decisions.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-service="flashpoint"><span class="tile-number">04</span><span class="tile-icon">◇</span><strong>Flashpoint</strong><small>A real workload gives the platform something to measure.</small></button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell">
      <div class="feature-card"><div class="card-kicker">PLANNED EXPERIMENTS</div><h3>Curiosity, with guardrails.</h3><p>Future services may include self-hosted applications, local AI tools, richer tracing, and more deliberate failure tests. They will stay personal, private by default, and observable from their first run.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>Self-hosted applications</span><span>Local AI</span><span>OpenTelemetry</span><span>Failure testing</span></div></div>
    </section>
  </main>

